// Title: Potentially Suspicious Named Pipe Created Via Mkfifo
// Sigma ID: 999c3b12-0a8c-40b6-8e13-dd7d62b75c7a
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-06-16 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects the creation of a new named pipe using the "mkfifo" utility in a potentially suspicious
//   location
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://dev.to/0xbf/use-mkfifo-to-create-named-pipe-linux-tips-5bbk
//   - https://www.mandiant.com/resources/blog/barracuda-esg-exploited-globally
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_mkfifo_named_pipe_creation_susp_location.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/mkfifo" and ProcessCommandLine contains " /tmp/"
